" IdeaVim for JetBrains IDEs (keymap: IntelliJ GNOME).
" Vim handles text editing; IDE actions use the IDE's own shortcuts
" (Alt-Enter, Shift-F6, Shift-Alt-7, Ctrl-Q, Shift Shift...).

" search and scrolling
set scrolloff=8
set hlsearch
set incsearch
set ignorecase
set smartcase

" Code navigation, LazyVim style: gd (declaration) is built into IdeaVim
" references, in the Find Usages panel (Vim's gr replaces a virtual character, rarely used)
nmap gr <Action>(FindUsages)
" implementations of an interface or method (Vim's gI inserts at column 1: 0i)
nmap gI <Action>(GotoImplementation)
" go to the declaration of the variable's type (Vim's gy does nothing)
nmap gy <Action>(GotoTypeDeclaration)
" go to super method or interface (not in LazyVim; Vim's gs only sleeps)
nmap gs <Action>(GotoSuperMethod)

" J joins lines the way the IDE does (strings, comments)
set ideajoin
" no beep
set visualbell

" Shortcut conflicts: who handles each Ctrl key (n-v = normal and visual,
" i = insert, a = all modes). Vim gets the key when its function is useful
" and the IDE action can be reached another way in two steps at most; the
" IDE gets it when Vim's function is redundant or the action is important.
" Each comment says how to reach what that key no longer does.
" ":action <ID>" runs any IDE action by name; :actionlist shows the IDs.
" Ctrl-M is left alone: in insert mode it is Enter. Scroll to center with zz.

" Vim everywhere
" increment number (IDE select all: Esc then ggVG)
sethandler <C-a> a:vim
" page up (IDE go to declaration: gd or Ctrl-click)
sethandler <C-b> a:vim
" page down (IDE find: Shift-Alt-3 or /)
sethandler <C-f> a:vim
" file info (IDE go to line: 42G or :42)
sethandler <C-g> a:vim
" jump forward (IDE implement methods: Alt-Enter or Alt-Insert)
sethandler <C-i> a:vim
" jump back; one normal command in insert (IDE override methods: Alt-Insert)
sethandler <C-o> a:vim
" redo; insert a register in insert (IDE replace: Shift-Alt-3, then open replace)
sethandler <C-r> a:vim
" tag stack back; indent in insert (IDE update project: Alt-` then Update)
sethandler <C-t> a:vim
" half page up; delete to line start in insert (IDE super method: Navigate menu or the gutter arrow)
sethandler <C-u> a:vim
" window commands; delete previous word in insert (IDE extend selection: :action EditorSelectWord)
sethandler <C-w> a:vim
" scroll up (IDE delete line: "_dd)
sethandler <C-y> a:vim
" escape (IDE code block start: [{)
sethandler <C-[> a:vim
" go to definition (IDE code block end: ]})
sethandler <C-]> a:vim

" Vim in normal/visual, IDE while typing
" half page down / duplicate line (from normal: i then Ctrl-D, or :t.)
sethandler <C-d> n-v:vim i:ide
" visual block / paste
sethandler <C-v> n-v:vim i:ide
" decrement number / cut
sethandler <C-x> n-v:vim i:ide

" IDE in normal/visual, Vim while typing
" type hierarchy / backspace
sethandler <C-h> n-v:ide i:vim
" commit / digraph, like Ctrl-K a' for á (commit from insert: Alt-0)
sethandler <C-k> n-v:ide i:vim

" IDE everywhere
" copy (Vim: cancel, same as Esc)
sethandler <C-c> a:ide
" recent files (Vim scroll one line: Ctrl-Down)
sethandler <C-e> a:ide
" insert live template (Vim: down / new line, same as j and Enter)
sethandler <C-j> a:ide
" find next (Vim: redraw; clear search highlight with :noh)
sethandler <C-l> a:ide
" go to class (Vim: down / completion, same as j and the IDE popup)
sethandler <C-n> a:ide
" parameter info (Vim: up / completion, same as k and the IDE popup)
sethandler <C-p> a:ide
" quick documentation (Vim: visual block, same as Ctrl-V)
sethandler <C-q> a:ide
" save all (Vim: nothing)
sethandler <C-s> a:ide
" undo (Vim: suspend, meaningless in the IDE)
sethandler <C-z> a:ide
